KA\004\009hdr_grid\004\007SIATKA\004\008hdr_fav\004\024NAJCZƒò≈öCIEJ WYBIERANE\004\009hdr_btns\004\016PRZYCISKI DOLNE\004\012hdr_tooltip\004\008TOOLTIP\004\011hdr_scroll\004\007SCROLL\004\011hdr_colors\004\007KOLORY\004\015hdr_panel_opts\004\013OPCJE PANELU\004\003en\004\021Automatic categories\020wYour shelf is empty. Plugin Shelf can add your installed plugins and sort them into categories for you. Choose a mode:\020jThe wizard adds plugins that aren't on the shelf yet (existing categories and tiles stay). Choose a mode:\004\016Add instruments\004\015Add JS effects\020/One version of each plugin (VST3 > CLAP > VST)\004\029Match icons from the library\020/REAPER COPY: skip categories deleted in REAPER\004\034Delete all categories and plugins\020·Delete ALL categories and plugins from the shelf?\010\010Your license, appearance and settings stay. The plugin actions will be removed from REAPER's action list. Data backup: user_plugins_3.x.lua.przed-czyszczeniem.bak\010\010Continue?\020`Plugins deleted: %d. The shelf is empty - you can fill it with the Automatic categories button.\004\014Fill in icons\020¶Tiles without an icon (including those whose icon file is gone from the folder) get one from the library when a matching one exists (file name like the plugin name).\0201Icons filled in: %d of %d tiles without an icon.\020ßAdds everything at once and creates the categories itself: from the categories REAPER knows for each plugin, or by name when there are none (EQ, Dynamics, Reverb...).\020ëLike AUTO, but asks about every plugin whether it belongs to the suggested category. Yes - next; No - pick another category or create a new one.\020{Copies the categories from REAPER's FX browser (with your changes and your own folders) together with the plugins in them.\004\008Not now\004\026Adding plugins... %d / %d\004\005Stop\004\016Plugin %d of %d\004)Does this plugin belong to the category:\004\004Yes\004\003No\004\012Skip plugin\004\021Yes to all remaining\004\007Finish\004(Which category should the plugin go to?\004\013New category\004\015Create and add\004\005Back\0201Plugins added: %d\010New categories: %d\010Skipped: %d\020DPlugins with no category in REAPER (added to ‚ÄúNo category‚Äù): %d\004\018Could not add: %d\020uDEMO version: %d plugins didn't fit the limit (categories and plugins per category). The full version adds them all.\020/DEMO version limit - this plugin wasn't added.\004\031This plugin couldn't be added.\020^No new plugins to add were found (they're all on the shelf already or hidden in the scanner).\020GREAPER's FX browser has no categories or folders with plugins to copy.\004\024Automatic categories...\004\020The shelf is empty.\004\017View: categories\004\017View: developers\020_Switches the bar between categories and developers (from plugin names, as in the scan window).\020_Developer view: click a tile to insert the plugin. Editing and sorting - in the category view.\004\010FX chains\004\006Other\020ëGlobal search ON: the search box inside a category searches all categories, like on the Home page. Global search OFF: only the current category.\020ãPopups (Options, Search plugins, Add plugin and others) no longer block the main window - you can keep several open and still click tiles.\020˝Deletion history: \034Undo\034 and \034History\034 buttons. Deleted plugins go back to their place in the category, several entries can be restored at once, and the history (last 20) is kept after the script is closed. Deleting selected tiles is undone as a whole.\020®Periodic backups: 6 backups every 30 minutes with date and time (Options > Maintenance, a \034Restore\034 button next to each). Closing the script no longer overwrites them.\020ÄQuick Switch: the default shortcut is Left Alt alone (Ctrl+Space clashed with a REAPER shortcut). You can change it in Options.\020pOn by default: window always on top, popups always on top and popups on the script's screen (Options > Window).\020oThe chain tooltip shows the effects read from the chain file - also for chains added from REAPER's chain list.\020èGlobal search: hovering a found plugin highlights its category in the bar, like on the Home page. The highlight colour is in Options > Colors.\020^Several selected tiles (Ctrl+click) can be dragged together to another place in the category.\020ìAdd plugin: a \034Browse...\034 button next to the action field - a list of \034Insert FX:\034 actions from the Action List. A tile can run any REAPER action.\020jOlder REAPER (e.g. 6.4): the plugin list is read from REAPER's files - scanning, presets and chains work.\020–Fixes: a tile without an icon keeps its text layout when it zooms; \034Remove from list\034 only on the Home page lists; docking by dragging no longer stops the script; colour sub-sections in Options are indented.\020ˇN\001\000\000\000\000\000\0003.7.8: category text color (Options > Colors, or right-click a category > Category color for just one); the chain buttons in Search plugins stick to the right edge of the window; after adding a chain the window stays on the Chains tab; the color picker is always on top; About: ReaPack address for updates and a link to all products.\020ˇ:\001\000\000\000\000\000\0003.7.3: the bottom bar now uses icons - hover for 1 s to see the description; the window and dialogs open instantly (previously about 2 s of waiting); warnings and questions always appear above the script windows; you can drag the main window out of the docker again - without the ‚ÄúEnd() too many times‚Äù error.\020ˇ\002\001\000\000\000\000\000\0003.7.2: windows and dialogs no longer flicker when moved or kept on top; the script window you click comes to the front. To dock the main window, drag it while holding Shift. The buttons at the bottom open and close their windows (open = highlighted button).\020ˇ \001\000\000\000\000\000\0003.7.1: plugins from Search plugins and from automatic categories are inserted on older REAPER too (e.g. 6.4), also in chains; chains from FX Chains subfolders work; the Auto-float switch decides whether a new plugin window opens; in the chain list a tooltip shows what is inside a chain.\020†Options > Window: popups open on the screen of the Plugin Shelf window (in its middle, then where you left them) - no more hunting for them on another monitor.\020ñRight-click on empty space: on the category bar it adds a new category, in the tile area it opens a menu with Search plugins / Add plugin to browser.\020åGlobal search switch next to Auto-float FX: when it's on, the search box inside a category searches all categories (like on the Home page).\020wAutomatic categories: AUTO, SemiAUTO and REAPER COPY - with the button on the empty shelf or in Options > Maintenance.\020=View switch next to Auto-float FX: categories or developers.\020âNew logo and a REAPER toolbar icon: \034Emelowsky - Plugin Shelf for REAPER (toolbar icon).zip\034 in the package (see the quick start guide).\020™Drag tiles: onto a category in the top bar to move them there (also several selected with Ctrl+click), within a category to change the order (the other tiles make room).\004\007Cancel\004\005Save\004\004Add\004\009Activate\004\008Refresh\004\016Refresh actions\004\012üìÅ Browse\004\010üìã Copy\020ˇã\001\000\000\000\000\000\000Refresh all automatically generated plugin actions? This is a FULL cleanup: it will remove ALL action files from the script folder (including orphaned ones, e.g. from older versions) and unregister them from REAPER, then recreate fresh actions for your current plugins. If you manually assigned a keyboard shortcut to any of them in REAPER, you will need to reassign it. This may take a moment.\020/Old files removed: %d\010Refreshed: %d\010Errors: %d\004\005Done\004\015Add to session\004\015Add to browser\004\021Add chain to browser\004\011(FX chain)\004\016Export settings\004\016Import settings\004\016Exported to:\010%s\004\027Could not export settings.\004!Select a settings file to import\020§This will OVERWRITE all current set